    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Twenty-Two Words, Five Landmines",
     "content": "Here is the actual request, verbatim:\n\n*Can you get me our readmission rate for last quarter before the Regence meeting? Just need the number. Thanks.*\n\nTwenty-two words. Now count the undefined terms.\n\n• **our** — the whole four-hospital system, or just this campus? The system rate and the campus rate differ by about two points every quarter.\n• **readmission** — return to inpatient status only, or does an ED visit count? Do planned readmissions count — the staged hip revision, the scheduled chemotherapy admission?\n• **rate** — over what denominator? Every discharge, or only discharges that were *eligible* to be readmitted? Patients who died in-house cannot come back.\n• **last quarter** — calendar or fiscal? And is a stay assigned to a quarter by its admission date or its discharge date? Those disagree on every stay that spans a quarter boundary.\n• **the number** — compared to what? A number with no benchmark and no confidence interval is a rumor.\n\nHere is how it usually goes: the analyst answers in eleven minutes, the number is quoted in a contract meeting, and four weeks later someone from finance runs it differently and gets a different answer. Now nobody trusts either number, and the credibility you spent two years building is gone in one email.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">THE REQUEST AS IT ARRIVES</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Five landmines hiding in twenty-two words</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"135\" width=\"940\" height=\"275\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,0.05)\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"185\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">From: CFO          Sent: Friday 4:51 PM</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Subject: readmission number for Monday</text><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"245\" x2=\"990\" y2=\"245\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"1\" opacity=\"0.4\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"293\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"21\">Can you get me our readmission rate for last</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"21\">quarter before the Regence meeting? Just need</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"367\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"21\">the number. Thanks.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"440\" width=\"940\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"495\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"505\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">1</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"482\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">our</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"518\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Four-hospital system, or just this campus?</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"560\" width=\"940\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"615\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"625\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">2</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"602\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">readmission</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"638\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Inpatient only? ED visits? Planned returns?</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"680\" width=\"940\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"735\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">3</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"722\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">rate</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"758\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">All discharges, or only eligible discharges?</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"800\" width=\"940\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"855\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"865\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">4</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"842\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">last quarter</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"878\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Fiscal or calendar? Admit date or discharge?</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"920\" width=\"940\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"975\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"985\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">5</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"962\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">the number</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"998\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Against which benchmark, for which decision?</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The five undefined terms buried in a routine analytics request"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Interrogate the Question First",
     "content": "Professional analysts do not start with the query. They start with a **specification** — six fields, all filled in, agreed in writing before a single line of SQL gets typed. It takes ten minutes and it is the highest-return ten minutes in the entire profession.\n\n• **Decision** — what will somebody actually *do* differently depending on the answer? If nothing changes either way, you have a curiosity, not a request, and it goes in the queue behind the work that moves something.\n• **Population** — precisely which encounters enter the denominator, and which are excluded and why. Every exclusion is a defensible choice or a thumb on the scale.\n• **Event** — precisely what counts in the numerator. Same rigor.\n• **Window** — which clock, anchored to which date, over which reporting period. Discharge date and admission date do not agree at quarter boundaries.\n• **Source and authority** — which system is the system of record for this field? The final coded abstract and the real-time ADT feed will disagree, and only one of them is defensible in a contract negotiation.\n• **Threshold** — what result would change the decision? Ask it out loud. If the answer is *nothing would change our position*, you have just saved yourself a week.\n\nWrite the spec. Send it back. Get a reply that says yes. That reply is the difference between an analyst and a report generator — and it is the artifact that protects you when the number is challenged six months later.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">THE ANALYTIC REQUEST SPEC</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">No query starts until all six fields are filled</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"135\" width=\"960\" height=\"125\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"95\" y=\"163\" width=\"245\" height=\"70\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"217\" y=\"207\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">DECISION</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">What changes based on the answer?</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Contract terms at the 11% penalty threshold</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"280\" width=\"960\" height=\"125\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"95\" y=\"308\" width=\"245\" height=\"70\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"217\" y=\"352\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">POPULATION</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Which stays enter the denominator?</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"373\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Adult inpatient, less deaths and acute transfers</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"425\" width=\"960\" height=\"125\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"95\" y=\"453\" width=\"245\" height=\"70\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"217\" y=\"497\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">EVENT</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">What counts in the numerator?</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"518\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Unplanned inpatient readmission, any cause</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"570\" width=\"960\" height=\"125\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"95\" y=\"598\" width=\"245\" height=\"70\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"217\" y=\"642\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">WINDOW</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"625\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Which clock, anchored where?</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"663\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">30 days from discharge date, Q2 index stays</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"715\" width=\"960\" height=\"125\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"95\" y=\"743\" width=\"245\" height=\"70\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"217\" y=\"787\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14b8a6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">SOURCE</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"770\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Which system is authoritative?</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"808\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Final coded abstract, not the live ADT feed</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"860\" width=\"960\" height=\"125\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"95\" y=\"888\" width=\"245\" height=\"70\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"217\" y=\"932\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">THRESHOLD</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"915\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">What result would change the call?</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"953\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Above 11% we renegotiate; below it we sign</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1040\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"21\">Ten minutes here saves a week of rework later</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The six-field specification every analytic request should carry before any query runs"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Worked: How 16.0% Becomes 9.4%",
     "content": "Mercy Regional, Q2. **2,400 adult inpatient discharges.** Within 30 days, **384** of those patients came back to the organization in some form. Watch the number move as each definitional choice gets made.\n\n**Method A — count every return.**\n384 / 2,400 = **16.0%**\n\n**Method B — unplanned inpatient readmissions only.** Of the 384, **96** were ED visits that never converted to an admission, and **48** were planned returns — staged procedures, scheduled chemotherapy.\n384 − 96 − 48 = **240** qualifying readmissions.\n240 / 2,400 = **10.0%**\n\n**Method C — clean the denominator too.** Of the 2,400 index stays, **120** ended in an in-house death (that patient cannot be readmitted) and **180** were transfers to another acute care hospital (disposition 02 — the receiving facility owns what happens next).\n2,400 − 120 − 180 = **2,100** eligible index stays.\nRemoving those 180 transfer stays also removes the **42** readmissions attached to them: 240 − 42 = **198**.\n198 / 2,100 = **9.4%**\n\nSpread: **6.6 percentage points** between the highest and lowest defensible answer, and the contract penalty sits at 11% — right in the middle. A transitional care program sized off Method A staffs for 384 events a quarter when the real, comparable figure is 198. That is roughly double the nurses, funded for a problem that size does not exist.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">ONE QUARTER, THREE METHODS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Mercy Regional Q2: 2,400 adult inpatient discharges</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"520\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"520\" x2=\"1010\" y2=\"520\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"187\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">18%</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"527\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">0%</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"218\" width=\"160\" height=\"302\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"470\" y=\"331\" width=\"160\" height=\"189\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"760\" y=\"342\" width=\"160\" height=\"178\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"268\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">16.0%</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"381\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">10.0%</text><text x=\"840\" y=\"392\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">9.4%</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"312\" x2=\"1010\" y2=\"312\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"8\"/><text x=\"1005\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"18\">11% contract penalty threshold</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"557\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"19\">METHOD A</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"557\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"19\">METHOD B</text><text x=\"840\" y=\"557\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"19\">METHOD C</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"590\" width=\"980\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"642\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">A - count every return</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"682\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">ED visits and planned readmits all included</text><text x=\"1000\" y=\"665\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"23\">384 / 2,400 = 16.0%</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"735\" width=\"980\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"787\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">B - unplanned inpatient only</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"827\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Drop 96 ED-only and 48 planned returns</text><text x=\"1000\" y=\"810\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"23\">240 / 2,400 = 10.0%</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"880\" width=\"980\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"932\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">C - clean the denominator too</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"972\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Remove 120 deaths and 180 acute transfers</text><text x=\"1000\" y=\"955\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"23\">198 / 2,100 = 9.4%</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1060\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"21\">Only Method A crosses the penalty threshold</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The same 2,400 discharges producing 16.0%, 10.0%, and 9.4% depending on definitions"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "What To Do With The Next Request",
     "content": "The next analytics request that reaches you — this week, probably — gets this treatment.\n\n1. **Do not open the query tool.** Not yet. The instinct to prove you are fast is the instinct that produces the wrong number quickly.\n\n2. **Fill the six-field spec.** Decision, population, event, window, source, threshold. Write it out. Leave blanks where you genuinely do not know, because the blanks are the questions you need to ask.\n\n3. **Send it back and name the exclusions out loud.** *I am excluding in-house deaths and acute transfers from the denominator — confirm that matches how Regence computes it.* Every exclusion is either a defensible methodological choice or a thumb on the scale, and the only way to tell is to say it in public.\n\n4. **Deliver the number with its context attached.** Never a bare percentage. Numerator, denominator, definition, benchmark, and an honest statement of uncertainty.\n\n5. **Publish the definition, not just the result.** Put the spec into a shared data dictionary so the next person who asks about readmissions gets your number, not a new one.\n\nThat reply-that-says-yes is the artifact that protects you when the number gets challenged in a meeting you are not in.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">YOUR INTAKE PROTOCOL</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Run this on the next request that reaches you</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"150\" width=\"920\" height=\"115\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"207\" r=\"32\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">1</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"198\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">Do not open the query tool</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Being fast is how you get to be wrong quickly</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"282\" width=\"920\" height=\"115\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"339\" r=\"32\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">2</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">Fill the six-field spec</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"367\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Decision, population, event, window, source, threshold</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"414\" width=\"920\" height=\"115\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"471\" r=\"32\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"482\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">3</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"462\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">Name every exclusion out loud</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"499\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">A silent exclusion is indistinguishable from a bias</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"546\" width=\"920\" height=\"115\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"603\" r=\"32\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"614\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">4</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"594\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">Never deliver a bare percentage</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"631\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Numerator, denominator, benchmark, uncertainty</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"678\" width=\"920\" height=\"115\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"735\" r=\"32\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"746\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">5</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"726\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">Publish the definition, not the result</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"763\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Put the spec in a data dictionary others reuse</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"840\" width=\"920\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"893\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"23\">THE ARTIFACT THAT PROTECTS YOU</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"940\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">A written spec with a reply that says yes.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"980\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Six months later, that email is your entire defense.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "A five-step intake protocol for the next analytics request that lands on your desk"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "A colleague reports Mercy Regional's Q2 readmission rate as 16.0% by dividing all 384 thirty-day returns by all 2,400 discharges. You notice that 120 of those 2,400 index stays ended in an in-house death. Which criticism of that denominator is most defensible?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "The denominator should be average daily census for the quarter rather than discharges",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Patients who died during the index stay could never be readmitted, so leaving them in the denominator biases the rate downward",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Leaving deaths in the denominator biases the rate upward and makes performance look worse than it is",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Readmissions should be expressed per 1,000 at-risk patient-days rather than as a percentage of stays",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "A patient who died during the index stay has exactly zero probability of being readmitted. Those 120 stays inflate the denominator without ever being able to contribute a numerator event, so the rate is biased downward: 240/2,400 = 10.0%, but 240/2,280 = 10.5% once deaths come out. The third option gets the mechanism right and the direction exactly backwards — a larger denominator makes a rate smaller, never larger.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Who actually belongs in the denominator?</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"150\" width=\"440\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">DEATHS LEFT IN</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">240</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"305\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"305\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"360\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">2,400</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">= 10.0%</text><rect x=\"580\" y=\"150\" width=\"440\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">DEATHS REMOVED</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">240</text><line x1=\"700\" y1=\"305\" x2=\"900\" y2=\"305\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"360\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">2,280</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"30\">= 10.5%</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"510\" width=\"940\" height=\"210\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"565\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"23\">THE MECHANISM</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"615\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">120 patients died during the index stay.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"653\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Their probability of readmission is exactly zero.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"693\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">They can only ever be denominator, never numerator.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"760\" width=\"940\" height=\"150\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"818\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"23\">BIGGER DENOMINATOR, SMALLER RATE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"868\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Leaving them in biases the rate downward.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"945\" width=\"940\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"1010\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"21\">Every exclusion is a claim you have to defend</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Removing ineligible index stays raises the rate from 10.0% to 10.5%"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "The Road From Here",
     "content": "You now know the shape of the problem: a question arrives underspecified, the data is not what its column names claim, and a decision worth millions gets made off whatever number you hand back. Everything in the next nineteen lessons is a tool for handling that responsibly.\n\nThe arc runs in eight stages.\n\n• **Design the study** — research questions, hypotheses, and the study designs that can and cannot support a causal claim.\n• **Protect the subjects** — IRB review, secondary use of PHI, de-identification, and the ethics that make health data different from every other kind of data.\n• **Describe the data** — distributions, central tendency, variability, skew, and what a mean hides that a median reveals.\n• **Infer from samples** — confidence intervals, p-values, statistical versus clinical significance, and choosing the right test instead of the familiar one.\n• **Model relationships** — correlation, regression, risk adjustment, and why an unadjusted comparison between two hospitals is almost always meaningless.\n• **Judge data quality** — accuracy, completeness, currency, consistency, granularity, and how to audit for each.\n• **Query and shape it** — joins, aggregation, filters, and reproducible data preparation.\n• **Show it and tell it** — honest visualization, dashboards that get used, and the narrative that actually changes a decision.\n\nNext lesson: how to turn a vague operational complaint into a research question sharp enough to answer — and the study designs that answer it.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">THE ROAD FROM HERE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Twenty lessons, eight stages, one craft</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"150\" width=\"480\" height=\"190\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"205\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"25\">1</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">DESIGN THE STUDY</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"265\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Research questions, hypotheses,</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">designs, sampling strategy</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"150\" width=\"480\" height=\"190\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"615\" cy=\"205\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"615\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"25\">2</text><text x=\"665\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">PROTECT THE SUBJECTS</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"265\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">IRB review, secondary use of PHI,</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">de-identification, research ethics</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"370\" width=\"480\" height=\"190\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"425\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"436\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"25\">3</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"435\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">DESCRIBE THE DATA</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Distributions, central tendency,</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">variability, skew, outliers</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"370\" width=\"480\" height=\"190\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"615\" cy=\"425\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"615\" y=\"436\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14b8a6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"25\">4</text><text x=\"665\" y=\"435\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#14b8a6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">INFER FROM SAMPLES</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Confidence intervals, p-values,</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">choosing the right test</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"590\" width=\"480\" height=\"190\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"645\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"656\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"25\">5</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">MODEL RELATIONSHIPS</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"705\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Correlation, regression,</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">risk adjustment, prediction</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"590\" width=\"480\" height=\"190\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"615\" cy=\"645\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"615\" y=\"656\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"25\">6</text><text x=\"665\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">JUDGE DATA QUALITY</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"705\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Accuracy, completeness, currency,</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">consistency, granularity</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"810\" width=\"480\" height=\"190\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"865\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"876\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"25\">7</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"875\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">QUERY AND SHAPE IT</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"925\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Joins, aggregation, filters,</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"960\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">reproducible data preparation</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"810\" width=\"480\" height=\"190\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"615\" cy=\"865\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"615\" y=\"876\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"25\">8</text><text x=\"665\" y=\"875\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">SHOW IT AND TELL IT</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"925\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Honest charts, dashboards,</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"960\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">and the story that changes minds</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1055\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"21\">Next: turning a complaint into a research question</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The eight-stage arc of the book, from study design to communicating the result"
     }
    }
