    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "A dashboard tile reads: \"Unit D infection rate 5.0% — WORST IN HOSPITAL.\" Unit D had 3 infections among 60 patients. What must you add before this tile goes in front of the board?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "A confidence interval. With 3 of 60 the 95% interval runs roughly 0% to 10.5%, which overlaps every other unit, so the ranking claim is not supported.",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "A 12-month trend line for Unit D, so the board can see whether the rate is rising or falling.",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "The raw count of 3 instead of the percentage, since percentages exaggerate small numbers.",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "A red background and a warning icon, so the board understands the severity at a glance.",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The tile makes a ranking claim that its sample size cannot support, and the confidence interval is what exposes that. The trend line is genuinely useful and therefore the most tempting distractor — but 12 monthly points from a unit with three annual events are even noisier, and a trend does not repair a comparison across units. Swapping to the raw count trades one error for another: counts without denominators cannot be compared across units of different size.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">SMALL NUMBERS, WIDE INTERVALS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">95% CI around an observed rate of 5.0%</text><line x1=\"486\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"486\" y2=\"760\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7,6\"/><text x=\"486\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"17\">observed 5.0%</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"267\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">n = 30</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"931\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"246\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"274\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"931\" y1=\"246\" x2=\"931\" y2=\"274\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"486\" cy=\"260\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><text x=\"565\" y=\"296\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">0.0% to 12.8%</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"377\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">n = 60</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"370\" x2=\"800\" y2=\"370\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"356\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"384\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"800\" y1=\"356\" x2=\"800\" y2=\"384\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"486\" cy=\"370\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><text x=\"500\" y=\"406\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">0.0% to 10.5%</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"487\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">n = 150</text><line x1=\"286\" y1=\"480\" x2=\"685\" y2=\"480\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"286\" y1=\"466\" x2=\"286\" y2=\"494\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"685\" y1=\"466\" x2=\"685\" y2=\"494\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"486\" cy=\"480\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><text x=\"486\" y=\"516\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">1.5% to 8.5%</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"597\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">n = 400</text><line x1=\"363\" y1=\"590\" x2=\"608\" y2=\"590\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"363\" y1=\"576\" x2=\"363\" y2=\"604\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"608\" y1=\"576\" x2=\"608\" y2=\"604\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"486\" cy=\"590\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><text x=\"486\" y=\"626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">2.9% to 7.1%</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"707\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">n = 1000</text><line x1=\"409\" y1=\"700\" x2=\"563\" y2=\"700\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"409\" y1=\"686\" x2=\"409\" y2=\"714\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"563\" y1=\"686\" x2=\"563\" y2=\"714\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"486\" cy=\"700\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><text x=\"486\" y=\"736\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">3.7% to 6.4%</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"760\" x2=\"1000\" y2=\"760\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">0</text><text x=\"314\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">2</text><text x=\"429\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">4</text><text x=\"543\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">6</text><text x=\"657\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">8</text><text x=\"771\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">10</text><text x=\"886\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">12</text><text x=\"1000\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">14</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"822\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Infection rate (%)</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"850\" width=\"1020\" height=\"200\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"20\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"908\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"21\">Three infections in 60 patients is 5.0%.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"948\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"21\">It is also consistent with 0% and with 10.5%.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"21\">The interval is the finding. Put it on the chart.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "How the 95% interval around a 5.0% rate narrows as the denominator grows"
     }
    }
